WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:03.703 line:0%
I think there's a lot of humor
in this show.

00:00:03.803 --> 00:00:05.271 line:0%
Yeah. I'm funny.

00:00:05.371 --> 00:00:07.206
You're very funny.
You're without filter,

00:00:07.306 --> 00:00:09.742
which causes my character
a lot of problems.

00:00:09.843 --> 00:00:10.810
(LAUGHTER)

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:13.380
♪ (LIVELY MUSIC PLAYS) ♪

00:00:16.015 --> 00:00:17.283
So, episode three starts

00:00:17.383 --> 00:00:20.786
<i> when I'm letting Lucia and Mia
 out of my room,</i>

00:00:20.886 --> 00:00:21.921
<i> and you see that.</i>

00:00:22.021 --> 00:00:23.289
Good morning!

00:00:23.389 --> 00:00:24.657
Morning.

00:00:24.757 --> 00:00:25.492
And I ask you...

00:00:26.659 --> 00:00:29.495
Please don't say anything
about any of this to Albie,
okay, Dad, please?

00:00:29.928 --> 00:00:31.364
Look at those cannolis.

00:00:31.464 --> 00:00:33.333
MICHAEL IMPERIOLI:<i> You have
 a bit of a loose tongue,</i>

00:00:33.433 --> 00:00:36.002
and I don't know if that's
deliberate or just accidental.

00:00:36.102 --> 00:00:37.637
Honest. I don't speak
with forked tongue.

00:00:37.737 --> 00:00:38.338
I guess so.

00:00:38.772 --> 00:00:41.240
I made a plan for us today.
You should come.

00:00:41.341 --> 00:00:43.143
-That's okay.
-She's coming.

00:00:44.811 --> 00:00:47.347
I think Dominic's fine
with Portia coming along.

00:00:47.447 --> 00:00:51.050
He's happy to see his son
make a connection with someone,

00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:53.920
<i> especially a smart,
 nice, young woman.</i>

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:55.254
I think that
my character's delighted

00:00:55.354 --> 00:00:58.257
to have a young,
attractive woman around.

00:00:58.357 --> 00:01:05.198
He's very concerned about
still being attractive to women
who are one third his age.

00:01:05.465 --> 00:01:07.567
(LAUGHS) He's a little bit
unrealistic.

00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:10.769
In other words, he's just
this common 82-year-old guy.

00:01:10.869 --> 00:01:13.706
He's not gonna go gentle
into that good night, not Bert.

00:01:13.806 --> 00:01:14.840
And I love him for that.

00:01:15.474 --> 00:01:17.376
Do we embarrass you, Albie?

00:01:18.077 --> 00:01:22.381
No, it's just,
I don't think you realize
how you sound sometimes.

00:01:22.881 --> 00:01:26.486
What Albie brings is a balance
to our point of view,

00:01:26.586 --> 00:01:29.022
and a perspective
that otherwise wouldn't exist,

00:01:29.122 --> 00:01:30.189
not in our world.

00:01:30.289 --> 00:01:32.424
<i> He's helping Bert
 to look at himself,</i>

00:01:32.525 --> 00:01:33.793
and he certainly is
helping your character.

00:01:33.893 --> 00:01:36.562
My character's learning
from both you and him.

00:01:36.662 --> 00:01:41.968
In some ways, he feels closer
to some of the ways you grew up,

00:01:42.068 --> 00:01:43.670
and in some ways,
he feels closer to Albie.

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:47.340
<i> And he doesn't want
 to make the same mistakes.</i>

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:49.241
He has made a lot of
the same mistakes you did,

00:01:49.341 --> 00:01:50.643
but he wants to be able
to transcend them.

00:01:50.743 --> 00:01:53.879
<i> And he's looking towards Albie
 to help him, in a way.</i>

00:01:53.979 --> 00:01:56.983
And he's kind of caught
between both of those places.

00:01:57.083 --> 00:01:58.317
I need to change.

00:01:58.918 --> 00:02:02.422
And so, I don't think
I'm gonna be able to meet up
at all this week.

00:02:02.855 --> 00:02:04.257
This is for the ladies.

00:02:13.233 --> 00:02:16.235
Jennifer's character
just tickles me to death.

00:02:16.335 --> 00:02:17.837
Yeah, I was gonna say
the same thing.

00:02:17.937 --> 00:02:19.806
<i> -She's funny and-- yeah.</i>
-F. MURRAY ABRAHAM:
<i> She's a real hoot.</i>

00:02:19.906 --> 00:02:22.041
She's a real hoot.
That's a good way to put it.

00:02:22.141 --> 00:02:24.144
She'd be the most fun, probably.

00:02:27.079 --> 00:02:28.781
I personally like
to go with the flow.

00:02:28.881 --> 00:02:32.518
I might have a couple things,
like I wanna do this,
I wanna see that.

00:02:32.618 --> 00:02:34.420
I don't like going
on tours very much

00:02:34.521 --> 00:02:36.855
or being with other people
that I don't know,

00:02:36.955 --> 00:02:38.224
like on some kind of tour.

00:02:38.324 --> 00:02:39.592
I find that kind of confining.

00:02:39.692 --> 00:02:41.160
But, you know, I always
do a little bit of research,

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:44.497
and make a point
of going to see some things
that are interesting.

00:02:47.733 --> 00:02:50.803
Boy, considering how many
clothes this guy is wearing,

00:02:50.904 --> 00:02:52.071
I'm not gonna carry that stuff.

00:02:52.171 --> 00:02:53.273
I don't mind checking luggage.

00:02:53.373 --> 00:02:54.908
Check it, baby.

00:02:58.510 --> 00:03:00.579
I travel a lot,
just like you do,

00:03:00.679 --> 00:03:03.449
and after a long trip,
you get up 5:00 in the morning.

00:03:03.549 --> 00:03:05.952
And that's a great time
to go out and see a city.

00:03:06.052 --> 00:03:07.786
-Yeah.
-ABRAHAM: You own the place.

00:03:07.887 --> 00:03:11.090
You walk around
and you get a pretty good idea
of your bearings.

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:12.458
That's the way I like to travel.

00:03:12.558 --> 00:03:13.325
Yeah.

00:03:13.859 --> 00:03:15.528
And then, you know,
in the afternoon, you collapse.

00:03:15.628 --> 00:03:18.431
Yeah, me too.
I'm an early riser.

